            <ArticleTitle>[Quantitative evaluation of coronarographic findings using a point scoring system].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>597-606</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For the quantification of pathologic changes of the coronary arteries a score system is shown which consists for each stenosis of two factors. One for the degree of the stenosis and one for the localisation. The latter is adjusted according to the perfusion type (right dominant), balanced, left dominant coronary perfusion). The left ventricular score also consists of two factors. One for the quality of dysfunction (hypokinesia, akinesia, paradoxical pulsation) and one for the localisation (seven segments of left ventricular wall).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
